-- Carolina Field Almanac station data - EUROPE. Generated - do not edit by hand.
-- v0.28 (team 2026-11-14). Same method as the U.S. and Canadian stations. Sources:
-- POLAND: daily weather WGEN (Richardson & Wright 1984) fitted to IMGW-PIB daily SYNOP records 1991-2020, calibrated to 1991-2020
--   monthly normals computed from those records (WMO-No.1203 5/3 rule; >= 24 of 30 years). Stations above 1000 m (mountain peaks) left out.
--   "Zrodlem pochodzenia danych jest Instytut Meteorologii i Gospodarki Wodnej - Panstwowy Instytut Badawczy" (data source: IMGW-PIB).
--   Hourly temperature shape / humidity / wind / sky: NOAA ISD 1991-2020 at the SYNOP station (nearest one with >= 24 years if short);
--   sky counted below 12,000 ft like a U.S. ASOS. Day-to-day dryness and wind: NOAA GSOD. Rain timing: IMGW hourly present-weather
--   reports. Thunder: IMGW daily thunderstorm hours on rainy days. Snow vs rain: IMGW daily precipitation type on rainy days Nov-Mar.
-- UK AND IRELAND (England, Scotland, Wales, Northern Ireland; Republic of Ireland): daily weather WGEN fitted to Met Office MIDAS Open
--   daily temperature and rain 1991-2020 (CEDA, Open Government Licence; contains public sector information licensed under the OGL),
--   normals computed as above. Republic of Ireland: Met Eireann daily data 1991-2020 (clidata.met.ie via data.gov.ie, CC BY 4.0).
--   Hourly / sky / dryness: NOAA ISD and GSOD at the nearest UK or Irish SYNOP station. Rain timing: ISD hourly present weather;
--   thunder and snow: GSOD flags at that station on the station's rainy days.
-- FRANCE (by region): daily weather WGEN fitted to Meteo-France daily climate data 1991-2020 (data.gouv.fr, Licence Ouverte v2.0;
--   source: Meteo-France), normals computed as above, stations at or below 1000 m thinned to 25 km apart (most complete kept;
--   team pick 2026-11-14). Thunder and snow: the station's own daily ORAG (thunderstorm) and NEIG (snow) records on rainy days.
--   Hourly / sky / dryness: NOAA ISD and GSOD at the nearest French SYNOP station. Rain timing: ISD hourly present weather.
-- GERMANY (by state): daily weather WGEN fitted to DWD Climate Data Center daily KL records 1991-2020 (opendata.dwd.de, CC BY 4.0;
--   source: Deutscher Wetterdienst), normals computed as above, stations at or below 1000 m. Hourly shape / humidity / wind / sky: NOAA ISD
--   at the nearest German SYNOP station with >= 24 years; dryness and wind: DWD daily max, vapour pressure and wind at the station. Rain timing: DWD hourly precipitation at the
--   same stations. Thunder: DWD daily weather phenomena on rainy days. Snow vs rain: DWD daily precipitation form on rainy days Nov-Mar.
